(Track B2 — mremap growth past 64 MB. A dynamic buffer is grown past 64 MB by
 appending a 4 KB chunk repeatedly, exercising repeated large no-copy mremap
 remaps. Asserts the buffer did not crash and that size and capacity are
 coherent, both exactly 64 MB at the final doubling boundary.)

a buffer called chunk.
a number called j is 1.
While j is less than or equal to 64,
  Append "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz_+" to chunk,
  Increment j.

a buffer called big.
a number called i is 1.
While i is less than or equal to 16384,
  Append chunk to big,
  Increment i.

If big's size is equal to 67108864 then,
  If big's capacity is equal to 67108864 then,
    print "ok".
  Otherwise,
    print "BUG: capacity".
Otherwise,
  print "BUG: size".